<head>
<no>2</no><heading guid="_95d24b90-b524-4306-9e52-97631957c1b7"
id="sec.2-he"><b>Commencement</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act commences on the date of
assent.</txt></block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_82cbd8e0-c360-45bf-9586-ea84c002a1cb"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_2cd1559e-91b9-480b-9748-db1cfacfc0df"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_14964ee2-803b-4fd8-acbc-6a24dcdc4c19"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_7a015300-450b-4ca4-8546-1da333357bb3"
id="sec.3-def.ACCC"><b><i>ACCC</i></b></defterm> means the Australian
Competition and Consumer Commission established under the <legref jurisd="CTH"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Trade Practices Act
1974</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_49a2b09f-6466-449f-ba0c-c6408fc2ccb6"
id="sec.3-def.ASIC"><b><i>ASIC</i></b></defterm> means the Australian
Securities and Investments Commission.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_b9ace031-3a55-4620-a5f3-1e7ebca19ca1"
id="sec.3-def.Foundation"><b><i>Foundation</i></b></defterm> means the Medical
Research and Compensation Foundation (ACN 095 924 137).</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_86b841b3-feca-4ec8-aa2f-695b2b021bc8"
id="sec.3-def.JamesHardieSpecialCommissionofInquiry"><b><i>James Hardie
Special Commission of Inquiry</i></b></defterm> means the Special Commission
of Inquiry that was commissioned, by Letters Patent dated 27 February 2004 and
30 June 2004, to inquire into and report on certain matters relating to the
establishment of the Foundation.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_ff118071-6a4a-4c8a-a360-0b5cd6d8ee64"
id="sec.3-def.record"><b><i>record</i></b></defterm> has the same meaning as
in the <legref refid="act-1998-017" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>State Records Act
1998</i></name></legref>.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_31538f4c-fb8b-4266-9206-8f1135ba63e2"
id="sec.3-def.transferredrecord"><b><i>transferred record</i></b></defterm>
means a record that ASIC has control of under Part 2.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0799d6e4-1ede-40a7-96f0-9998a6528dc6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Notes included in this Act do not form part of
this Act.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 3:</b> Am 2004 No 90,
Sch 1 [1].</txt></content>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bb517233-580e-491c-b63b-d06b9729b32e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 2</b></no><heading guid="_d1c53859-5739-4407-aa3e-eed6e1ca277e"
id="pt.2-he"><b>Transfer of records to ASIC</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b8583bcb-4c6b-45e8-897b-f871c2084f18"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_9e0986a8-5941-4e76-856e-ed6c9749a109"
id="sec.4-he"><b>ASIC entitled to control of records of James Hardie Special
Commission of Inquiry</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ed00fa0e-7b49-40f0-b718-d336a4f4e1cf"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">ASIC is, by force of this section, entitled to
control of any record that was made, kept or received by the James Hardie
Special Commission of Inquiry that ASIC, in the performance of its functions
or exercise of its powers under Commonwealth law, requests a public office
entitled to control of the record under section 7 of the <legref
refid="act-1998-017" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>State Records Act 1998</i></name></legref> to provide or
make available to it.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ce63df1d-fa49-4105-9f3a-b2b17fd65f80"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">ASIC may give possession or custody, for any
purpose it considers appropriate in the performance of its functions or
exercise of its powers under Commonwealth law, of any record that it has in
its control under this Part to the ACCC or any other person, whether within or
outside New South Wales.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e50332f9-e3ad-4117-8858-2ba6ee0a0963"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">For the purposes of this section, an entitlement
of ASIC to control of a record is an entitlement to possession and custody of
the record (including by having it in the possession or custody of some other
person whether within or outside New South Wales).</txt></block></tier>

<note type="legtext" guid="_41f5b421-3309-45db-964f-1f5f9bed1906"
id="sec.4-note"><heading guid="_7798af46-46ed-4d99-b458-1d7e35b6d42b"
id="sec.4-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">Under section 127 (4) of the <legref jurisd="CTH"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Australian Securities and
Investments Commission Act 2001</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth, the
Chairperson of ASIC can authorise the use or disclosure of information ASIC
has been given in connection with the performance of its functions or the
exercise of its powers to enable or assist a government, or an agency (such as
the US Securities Exchange Commission), of a foreign country to perform a
function, or exercise a power, conferred by a law in force in that foreign
country.</txt></block></note>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 4:</b> Am 2004 No 90,
Sch 1 [2].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_83500dfa-3ac4-46e6-916b-587b2b99e2ca"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_92845d00-d552-48c8-a3e3-c3a9e6cafece"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Public office responsible for records to transfer them to
ASIC</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_97f12968-2980-47d1-ad21-7030f0b40655"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The public office entitled to control of a record
must provide or make the record available to ASIC as soon as practicable after
the request referred to in section 4 is made.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_d00d07d3-c0df-44c7-a117-ed17f3adc2f9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If the public office has an electronic version of
the record concerned it must ensure that an electronic copy of that electronic
version is provided or made available to ASIC as soon as practicable after the
request for the record is made.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_35b452fd-7dae-4be7-9b75-3520aa93f7bb"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_ed30adef-233c-497b-8e1f-428006e3c9ed"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Retention and return of transferred
records</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7372cd1a-701a-47d3-9b4e-1a468cbf2bae"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">ASIC may retain control of a record provided or
made available to it under section 5 for so long as ASIC considers, in
relation to the performance of its functions or exercise of its powers under
Commonwealth law, that it is desirable to do so.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f1f9e44b-9f57-431d-b236-9fce0dc430e6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The public office that provided or made the
record available to ASIC must take control of a record ASIC no longer wishes
to retain if requested to do so by ASIC.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3ef18688-8099-4993-bbd1-ee472dd48687"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_a0105bfc-37fb-43e6-91cc-c4b0970ab28a"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Use of transferred records</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The provision or making available of a record to
ASIC, or giving of possession or custody by ASIC to the ACCC or any other
person, under this Part operates, by force of this section, to prevent any
person from objecting to the use by ASIC, the ACCC or other person of the
record, or the disclosure of any matter contained in the record to ASIC, the
ACCC or other person, on the following grounds:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_155847d7-6f80-4810-bd9e-93d8953262e1" id="sec.7-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">that the record is or contains a privileged
communication passing between a legal practitioner (in his or her capacity as
a legal practitioner) and a person for the purpose of providing or receiving
legal professional services or that the use or disclosure of the record or any
matter contained in it would be a breach of an express or implied obligation
(whether or not arising under law) not to disclose the record or
matter,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_962bde2f-79b1-40fb-a3d0-76e54caddf3f" id="sec.7-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">that the record was produced to the James Hardie
Special Commission of Inquiry under compulsion of
law.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>

<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Am 2004 No 90,
Sch 1 [3] [4].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_03a7e619-7bfb-4127-aaee-5da7aff996f0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_d8b3ddaa-7d0b-428c-9e47-a30af47d1c13"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Use and admissibility in proceedings of transferred
records</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3685da99-7eb1-4d42-8d9a-c03083d6004a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A transferred record is to be treated for the
purposes of any law of the State as if it were a record that ASIC had lawfully
obtained, or given into the possession or custody of the ACCC or any other
person, in the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers
under Commonwealth law. Accordingly, nothing in any law of the State prevents
the use of such a record in any proceedings or renders the record inadmissible
if it would be able to be used or would be admissible in proceedings had any
law of the Commonwealth applied to or in respect of it.</txt></block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_bf56b44b-81f5-4616-a2cf-b00098ae2ffb"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In particular, sections 23 and 31 (2) of the
<legref refid="act-1983-090" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Special Commissions of Inquiry Act 1983</i></name></legref>
do not prevent or restrict:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_cc7d678c-8b83-4c74-a1e6-67ae0a62871f" id="sec.8-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the provision or making available to ASIC of any
record under this Part, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b1557152-6e02-4906-b9bc-2347871626f2" id="sec.8-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the publication or use by ASIC of a transferred
record, or of matter in or referred to in a transferred record, in connection
with the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers under any
Commonwealth law, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_69703816-d5f9-4105-8473-b05fe8d5bd5a" id="sec.8-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the giving into the possession or the custody of
the ACCC or any other person of any record under this Part,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_730b88b0-cb81-40de-ba54-28cf06bf966a" id="sec.8-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the publication or use by the ACCC or other
person of the record, or of matter in or referred to in the record, in
connection with the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers
under any law.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<note type="legtext" guid="_e381978a-31db-4989-8aaa-7b7f5eea8dbf"
id="sec.8-ssec.2-note"><heading guid="_5c22ec1f-d696-4955-a908-06be40fe6562"
id="sec.8-ssec.2-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">Section 23 limits the admissibility in any NSW
civil or criminal proceedings against a person of an answer made or book,
document or writing produced by the person as a witness to or before the James
Hardie Special Commission of Inquiry. Section 31 (2) makes it an offence to
contravene a direction given by the Commissioner preventing publication of
evidence given before the Commissioner or of matters contained in documents
lodged with the Commission.</txt></block></note>
</tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_03c5ae6d-536e-4c63-b70a-530944b2db65"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Except as provided by this section, nothing in
this Part affects the operation of section 23 or 31 (2) of the <legref
refid="act-1983-090" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Special Commissions of Inquiry Act 1983</i></name></legref>
in relation to the transferred records.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b1d2289b-c674-40b4-9b7e-0f73707e3043"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">If a question arises with respect to the
admissibility of a transferred record in any proceedings before a court in
which Part 3.10 of the <legref refid="act-1995-025" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Evidence Act 1995</i></name></legref>
is not applicable, the court may order that the record be produced to it and
may inspect the record for the purpose of determining the
question.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 8:</b> Am 2004 No 90,
Sch 1 [5] [6].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_44172e79-bba9-4593-ad8d-40e19b1cced0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_620092fa-bac0-4d9b-bf7e-37d46681e983"
id="sec.9-he"><b>No contravention of section 21 of <legref
refid="act-1998-017" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>State Records Act
1998</i></name></legref></b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Part has effect despite section 21 of the
<legref refid="act-1998-017" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>State Records Act
1998</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7ec0285b-9e1b-4a8a-af94-7688b40073f1"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 3</b></no><heading guid="_7f781c5d-ec59-48c7-8d99-f21cd8e03426"
id="pt.3-he"><b>Facilitation of certain civil
proceedings</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.10">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_aa3b84c6-682a-43d9-8ad3-71a9de55572a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.10"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>10</no><heading guid="_59cf5835-6586-4317-a7dc-2565dc64f55d"
id="sec.10-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Part:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_6652a34e-04df-4f0c-8a7a-59b901106bb1"
id="def.civilproceedings"><b><i>civil proceedings</i></b></defterm> includes
interlocutory or similar proceedings but does not include proceedings relating
to the imposition of a civil penalty.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_d4adc96b-b398-4da5-bc70-799bd7c3473a"
id="def.facilitatedparty"><b><i>facilitated party</i></b></defterm>
means:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_377d0def-5b21-4e6a-a7df-08817a5517a0" id="sec.10-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the Foundation,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_01a5603f-9b9b-4f5a-a452-d8efea22d11c" id="sec.10-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">Amaca Pty Limited (ACN 000 035
512),</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_a73e2fcc-8573-4622-95ee-b162b12631e3" id="sec.10-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">Amaba Pty Limited (ACN 000 387
342),</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ed3cd989-e257-4f32-959b-8e3daadb44c5" id="sec.10-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any other body or person (whether of the same or
a different kind) prescribed by the regulations.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_97c1f177-9873-4db1-82b8-ffb05169be30" id="def.NSWcourt"><b><i>NSW
court</i></b></defterm> has the same meaning as it has in the <legref
refid="act-1995-025" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Evidence Act
1995</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.11">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b4aa0fde-6a66-4e66-a07b-6ca23be5876d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>11</no><heading guid="_1a26cac3-8dd6-4e97-baa7-33a6e425b5c1"
id="sec.11-he"><b>Application of Part</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_2ebbea43-9184-400a-960c-795489a8abf3"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Attorney General may, if the Attorney General
considers it appropriate to do so in the public interest, by order published
in the Gazette, declare that this Part applies to and in respect of civil
proceedings in a NSW court specified in the order.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_52dc0771-6ecc-4ed6-bbb1-165a0c38d8bd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An order under this section may be made only if a
facilitated party advises the Attorney General that it intends to seek to
adduce evidence of an answer made, or record produced, by a witness to or
before the James Hardie Special Commission of Inquiry in the proceedings
concerned.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.11-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e5cd00c2-d52e-44f4-b843-2df74b892ca7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.11-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An order or purported order under this section
cannot be challenged, reviewed or called into question in any proceedings
before a NSW court, and a NSW court cannot prevent any such proposed order
from being made.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.12">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6ac4f773-a039-4536-b784-b03df71dc00e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>12</no><heading guid="_cd2ca831-7da0-470a-ad76-ca65baf4315b"
id="sec.12-he"><b>Retention and use of records</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.12-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a94c74e5-308d-40e8-97b7-d44d56af7e7f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A record produced by a witness to or before the
James Hardie Special Commission of Inquiry in the possession of a facilitated
party on the commencement of this Act may be retained and used by the
facilitated party for the purposes of proceedings to and in respect of which
this Part applies.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.12-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1318de2b-2fd7-435b-9a17-c3209ce5a516"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.12-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The use or retention of such a record does not,
for the purposes of the <legref refid="act-1983-090" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Special Commissions of Inquiry Act
1983</i></name></legref> or any other law, constitute contempt of
court.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.13">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a20953cb-3980-407e-bbc2-ed0fa5632cae"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>13</no><heading guid="_cacac66a-073c-4424-b794-7ea795e11baa"
id="sec.13-he"><b>Admissibility and use of certain evidence in proceedings to
which this Part applies</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f12d8161-cc7a-47bc-9367-caa39ada47e7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An answer made, or record produced, by a witness
to or before the James Hardie Special Commission of Inquiry is admissible in
evidence in proceedings to and in respect of which this Part applies
(including being admissible against the person who made the answer or produced
the record to or before that Inquiry).</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_ec4bac90-3ace-4838-9c76-effd009a5cc9"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) applies even if a person would be
excused from answering the question or producing the record:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_75c4637e-756f-41cd-acbe-7eb6ad29ce29" id="sec.13-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">on the ground (whether arising under the <legref
refid="act-1995-025" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Evidence Act 1995</i></name></legref> or any other law) that
the answer to the question, or the record, is or contains a privileged
communication passing between a legal practitioner (in his or her capacity as
a legal practitioner) and a person for the purpose of providing or receiving
legal professional services, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_08148b65-d4cc-42be-8cfc-ca5e64c9df83" id="sec.13-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">on the ground that the answer to the question, or
the record, would disclose a protected confidence within the meaning of
Division 1A of Part 3.10 of the <legref refid="act-1995-025" jurisd="NSW"
type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Evidence Act
1995</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_1d23608a-e4d6-4320-ad7d-6561292a1c71"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) applies despite section 23 (2) of
the <legref refid="act-1983-090" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Special Commissions of Inquiry Act 1983</i></name></legref>
but evidence is not admissible under that subsection against a natural person
if it may incriminate or tend to incriminate the person.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.13-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_5b7db45b-6edd-427c-9019-442057d25b70"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.13-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section does not operate to render
admissible in proceedings to and in respect of which this Part applies
evidence that would not be admissible apart from section 23 (2) of the <legref
refid="act-1983-090" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Special Commissions of Inquiry Act 1983</i></name></legref>
and this section.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.14">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_31b2a4eb-c738-4e95-a11d-a9ec8a337081"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>14</no><heading guid="_dde62101-a66f-4f66-b164-d331728398bb"
id="sec.14-he"><b>Directions preventing or restricting publication of evidence
not to apply</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_878cee14-a226-4c86-a2ee-a3ece950d8b0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Paragraph 2 of the direction given by the
Commissioner of the James Hardie Special Commission of Inquiry on 17 September
2004 does not prevent or restrict publication of matters contained in any
document referred to in that paragraph in or for the purposes of proceedings
to and in respect of which this Part applies.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.14-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_81680f1d-49e5-49c3-a998-2610422db552"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.14-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">No action or penalty lies against a person who
publishes a matter referred to in subsection (1) in or for the purposes of
proceedings to and in respect of which this Part applies on the ground that
the person has breached any express or implied obligation (whether or not
arising under law) not to disclose the matter.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</level>


<level type="part" id="pt.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_81f22b2c-6eb4-44d6-8e45-4e6bf6ce7343"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="pt.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no><b>Part 4</b></no><heading guid="_38bb8151-708f-4ebf-b563-b984e3db5731"
id="pt.4-he"><b>Miscellaneous</b></heading></head>

<level type="clause" id="sec.15">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fe335bff-e5ce-4408-abe0-f9ddadf04967"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.15"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>15</no><heading guid="_dc6a1f13-5d77-47cf-8181-fc74bbac6eb5"
id="sec.15-he"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.15-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b71b6cb9-4aa5-431c-8788-7d731c1a5dc7"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.15-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations, not
inconsistent with this Act, for or with respect to any matter that by this Act
is required or permitted to be prescribed or that is necessary or convenient
to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.15-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3237acc1-2dc8-481e-aac5-0002dbe4745e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.15-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In particular, the regulations may provide that
section 31 (2) of the <legref refid="act-1983-090" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Special Commissions of Inquiry Act
1983</i></name></legref> does not apply, to the extent specified in the
regulations, in relation to a direction given in relation to any particular
record or class of records.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.16">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_80aa0856-a12f-422a-90c9-e473010dd0ba"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.16"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>16</no><heading guid="_cf2cb994-1d7c-4dcd-97ef-76b5c5ad3d6d"
id="sec.16-he"><b>Savings and transitional provisions</b></heading></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Schedule 1 has effect.</txt></block>

